# 14. REQUIRED ACCEPTANCE TESTS

Before declaring the application complete, launch the actual running application and verify the following.

### Visual and gameplay tests

- All 64 country tokens spawn with the correct flags.
- No token uses an emoji, generic placeholder or unrelated flag.
- The arena retains its intended geometry and readable visual hierarchy.
- Collision and rotation behaviour remain stable during extended gameplay.
- Hazard warnings match the actual opening time.
- A fully fitting token physically falls through and is counted only once.
- Partial rim overlap does not cause arbitrary elimination.
- The match never declares a winner prematurely.
- Winner announcements, cumulative wins and next-match transitions work.
- Horizontal and vertical layouts are separately composed and inspected at their target dimensions.

### Audio tests

- Every confirmed elimination produces an audible announcement with the correct country name.
- Remaining counts spoken by the announcer match the simulation.
- Speech, music, impacts and countdown effects are mixed correctly.
- No persistent audio overlap, excessive collision spam or repeated stale announcement occurs.
- The actual stream/capture includes speech and effects.

### YouTube integration tests

- OAuth authorization succeeds against a configured channel.
- The correct active broadcast and live chat are identified.
- Real chat messages are received and deduplicated.
- A valid country support command changes the correct counter or support state.
- Supported membership and fan-funding events are correctly categorized.
- Subscriber monitoring reports only events established by available real data.
- Expired credentials, network interruptions and quota exhaustion produce recoverable errors.
- Demo events cannot accidentally be presented as real events in live mode.

### Deployment tests

- The public app can be deployed with a documented environment configuration.
- Persistent data survives application restarts.
- Secret credentials are not exposed to the frontend.
- OBS output is usable, or the cloud renderer passes a real encoder connectivity test.
- Audio and video remain synchronized.
- The application reports honest, observable stream status.

Capture actual screenshots and a demonstration recording. Inspect the output rather than relying only on source code or automated tests.

